From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Patryk Kowalczyk <papyszoo@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 12:07:21 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] PS5: the Extended Memory pack starts off

BetterVR 1.0.0's code and the pack's own text say it is for mods that need it (DrawDistance's Extreme and Ultra
presets); on, it moved the game's heaps and the first console run's allocator returned 0. The pack stays in the
Graphic packs list to turn on.
---
 .../graphicPacks/BreathOfTheWild/Mods/ExtendedMemory/rules.txt  | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/resources/graphicPacks/BreathOfTheWild/Mods/ExtendedMemory/rules.txt b/resources/graphicPacks/BreathOfTheWild/Mods/ExtendedMemory/rules.txt
index 3040940..ffad01b 100644
--- a/resources/graphicPacks/BreathOfTheWild/Mods/ExtendedMemory/rules.txt
+++ b/resources/graphicPacks/BreathOfTheWild/Mods/ExtendedMemory/rules.txt
@@ -4,7 +4,7 @@ name = Extended Memory
 path = "The Legend of Zelda: Breath of the Wild/Mods/Extended Memory"
 description = Adds an extra 2GB of emulated RAM.|Only enable this if a mod you want to use requires this since it'll use more RAM.
 version = 6
-default = true
+default = false
 
 [RAM]
 mapping0 = 0x10000000-0xA0000000 # extend MEM2 region (default range is 0x10000000-0x50000000)
